## Resume Context (2026-08-02 Session, part 5 — sync --from-status crash fix + test coverage)

Fixed a real crash in `atlas sync --from-status`: a frontmatter-format `.STATUS` with a non-numeric
`priority:` (e.g. `priority: P1` — found live in `scribe/.STATUS` and
`_worktrees/scribe-fix-vitest-watch/.STATUS`) stored the raw string, and `summarize()`'s
`Math.max(1, "P1")` → `NaN` → `byPriority[NaN]` undefined → `TypeError: Cannot read properties of
undefined (reading 'push')`. Fix in `StatusFileParser.js` (2 layers): frontmatter `priority` now
coerces like the markdown/bare-YAML formats (`parseInt || 3`, raw label preserved as `priorityLabel`),
and `summarize()` buckets any non-finite priority to 3. Regression coverage added: +57 lines in
`test/unit/adapters/gateways/StatusFileParser.test.js` (new `parse() - Frontmatter format` describe +
summarize non-numeric-priority test), new `test/e2e/sync-from-status.e2e.test.js` (4 CLI tests), new
`test/dogfood/sync-from-status.sh` (5 isolated-HOME checks, wired as `test:dogfood:sync`). Verified:
gateway suites 112/112, e2e 117/117, dogfood 5/5, real-world rescan of `~/projects/dev-tools` → 36
files, zero NaN priority keys; eslint clean. Docs updated (CHANGELOG `[Unreleased]`, WHAT-S-NEW,
STATUS-SCHEMA, CLI-REFERENCE, ARCHITECTURE, ROADMAP). Committed on `dev` (parser + tests + e2e +
dogfood + package.json + docs).

