**Two verification practices worth noting for future dashboard-hook work:** (1) a planted-defect
check on the freshly-written `useNudges` test suite found it did NOT actually cover the poll/ack
race it claimed to (a plausibly-named test exercised a different failure path) — added a real race
test using `jest.useFakeTimers()` scoped to that one test only (advances the 10s `setInterval`
deterministically while manual `Promise` control still orders the resolution), confirmed it fails
against the planted defect and passes against the fix. (2) A live E2E (`atlas nudge add` → real
`launchd` fire → real `atlas dash` render → real `a` keypress → `atlas nudge ls` confirms acked)
caught nothing new this time, but is what caught both of #114's real bugs originally — this is now
the dashboard's first write path, so the same standard applied here.

PR #118 merged to `dev` (`2099a2b`), worktree/branch cleaned up. Doc audit afterward found 4 real
