## Resume Context (2026-08-01 Session, part 1 — #114 wall-clock nudges + `atlas day`, v0.17.0 RELEASED)

Session closed out: v0.17.0 published (PR #117 merged `ede0d5c`), Homebrew tap PR #198 auto-merged and verified (correct SHA256), docs site confirmed serving v0.17.0 content, CI green on `main`, `dev` fast-forward-synced. Session report generated and published as an Artifact: `.remember/session-reports/session-report-2026-08-01.html`.


Full spec-to-ship cycle in one session: `/craft:brainstorm 114 and grill` → adversarial review killed the original `mcp__scheduled-tasks` approach (only fires while some Claude app is open — confirmed via its own tool description, not assumption) → redesigned around `launchd` + `osascript` → `SPEC-cross-surface-nudges-and-day-activity-2026-08-01.md` (v2.2, 4 review rounds) → `ORCHESTRATE-cross-surface-nudges-and-day-activity.md` (4 phases) → feature worktree → `/agent-skills:build auto` through all 4 phases → PR #116 → code review (self-run) found 3 issues, fixed → CI green → squash-merged to `dev` (`467d913`) → worktree/branches cleaned up.

Ships `atlas nudge {add,fire,ack,rm,ls}` (wall-clock reminders via `launchd`, fire even with every Claude surface closed; state shared cross-surface via `~/.claude/guards.json`'s new `nudges.wall-clock` key, deliberately NOT routed through the storage-branching repository pattern — see `GuardsFileNudgeStore` gateway) and `atlas day [--date] [--format table|json]` (multi-repo commit + `.STATUS`-diff + session-minutes provider across `r-packages/research/teaching/dev-tools`, feeds savant's `research-day-log` skill).

**Manual E2E surfaced two real bugs unit tests couldn't have caught** (documented in the PR body with full transcripts): (1) launchd's default PATH (`/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin`) can't resolve a Homebrew `node` via atlas.js's `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang — job exited 127 silently; fixed by invoking `process.execPath` directly as `ProgramArguments[0]`. (2) A fired nudge produced no banner even though `osascript` exited 0 — isolated via a manual interactive `osascript` test to a macOS setting, not code: System Settings → Notifications → Script Editor had **Alert Style set to None** (silently logs to Notification Center history only, no error anywhere). Documented as a setup prerequisite in `CLI-REFERENCE.md`.

**Code review (self-run via `/review 116`) found and fixed 3 further issues** before merge: an unlocked read-modify-write race on `guards.json` (added `withGuardsLock()` — atomic lock file, stale-PID reclaim, write-then-rename for atomicity), unescaped XML interpolation in the generated launchd plist (added `escapeXml()`), and `Nudge`'s constructor not validating `id` format (a hand-edited/corrupted `guards.json` entry could otherwise traverse `LaunchdNudgeScheduler`'s plist path — restricted to `[A-Za-z0-9_-]+`).

Along the way, also found and fixed a real git bug: a bare `git log --since=YYYY-MM-DD` defaults time-of-day to *now* (wall-clock at command-run time), not midnight — silently excludes same-day commits earlier than current time. Fixed by appending `' 00:00:00'` to both `--since`/`--until` in `GitGateway`'s new date-range methods.

93 suites / 1597 tests passing, lint clean. Issue #114 will auto-close on the next `dev → main` release (GitHub only auto-closes linked issues on merge to the *default* branch, not `dev`). Fast-follow already filed: #115 (surface fired-but-unacked nudges in `atlas dash`'s `NowView`, deferred deliberately — v1's delivery guarantee is the OS notification, not the dashboard).

