## Resume Context (2026-07-21 Session — demos.yml branch-protection fix, PRs #109-112)
Docs-site sidebar/theme redesign work from the prior session (PR #108) surfaced a pre-existing bug: `demos.yml`'s "Update GIFs in Repository" job did a direct `git push` to protected `main`. Fixed in two real-world-verified layers (each layer's failure was only discoverable by actually running the workflow, not by review): (1) PR #109 — bot-branch + `gh pr create` + `gh pr merge --auto`, mirroring the pattern already used for `homebrew-release.yml`; this alone still failed in production because the default `GITHUB_TOKEN` cannot open PRs on this repo (`can_approve_pull_request_reviews: false`). (2) PR #110 — added a GitHub App token (`actions/create-github-app-token@v1`, scoped to `repositories: atlas`) to mint the PR-creation credential, chosen over flipping the repo-wide permission setting. Real E2E run (29803662526) confirmed the App token works (opened PR #111) but surfaced a third bug: `gh pr merge --auto` errors with "Pull request is in clean status" when there are no pending checks left to wait for by the time the step runs. (3) PR #112 — falls back to a plain `gh pr merge --squash` when `--auto` fails. PR #111 (the auto-generated demo GIFs from the E2E run) merged directly. All four PRs (#109-112) CI-green, leak-scanned, merged dev→main same session; `dev`/`main` confirmed in sync (main's tip is a merge commit with dev's tip as ancestor). Next real E2E of the PR #112 fallback path itself will only occur on a future tape-file or workflow-file change.

## Focus: Two releases shipped back-to-back this session. v0.15.0 — XDG Base Directory support (`resolveConfigDir()`, `atlas migrate --xdg`, `doctor` nudge). v0.16.0 — ADHD-friendly docs-site redesign (PR #106): 7-tab nav collapsed to Home + 4 color pills + sidebar search (`overrides/partials/tabs.html`); section-color sidebar theming via `data-atlas-section` body attribute (`section-nav.js`); single-open sidebar accordion (required dropping `navigation.sections` — it force-expands L2 groups via CSS, silently defeating the checkbox collapse); homepage 6-card grid + chip-row principles; off-white/near-black + 16.5px/1.65 type; extended reduced-motion coverage. Two real bugs found and fixed during live dogfooding (not just build-check): pill nav dead-links (`children[0]` can be a section with no `.url` — needed a recursive first-leaf resolver) and a no-op accordion (traced to `navigation.sections`' CSS override). Also fixed atlas's `homebrew-release.yml` (direct push to protected tap `main` → PR + auto-merge) and cleared a stale Homebrew formula `revision 1` left over from the v0.15.0 caveats fix.
